\begin_layout Standard
The main objective of this doctoral project was to develop the skills required
 to prepare thin cross sections of crystalline material such that they could
 be characterised by high resolution scanning transmission electron microscopy
 (STEM).
 Subsequently, this technique was then applied to a range of novel structures
 composed of different two dimensional materials such as graphene.
